From: Kacper Goc <11682528+BurninChrome@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:54:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] HID: asus-ec: add ASUS EC hotkeys and keyboard backlight
 driver (Vivobook S15)

On Snapdragon based ASUS laptops the keyboard is an I2C HID device which
also carries vendor report 0x5A to and from the embedded controller. The
EC reports the Fn hotkeys through it and accepts feature reports for the
keyboard backlight (5A BA C5 C4 <0..3>) and Fn-lock (5A D0 4E <0|1>).

This driver binds to the keyboard instead of hid-generic, keeps the
regular hidinput and hidraw interfaces and adds:
- asus::kbd_backlight LED (0..3) with brightness_hw_changed, so that
  UPower/GNOME show the slider and the OSD for Fn+F4,
- Fn+Esc toggling the EC Fn-lock (also /sys/.../fn_lock),
- Fn hotkeys: brightness, mic mute, emoji, MyASUS, fan profile, etc.,
- backlight off on suspend, EC re-init and state restore on resume.

Based on the v1 driver by Alexandru Marc Serdeliuc for the Zenbook A14
(0B05:0220), "[PATCH] HID: asus: add new Asus EC hid device for keyboard
backlight and FN HotKeys", linux-input, 2025-12-21 (not merged; the
maintainer asked to fold it into hid-asus in v2, not posted as of
2026-10-09), and on the HID-BPF program by Icecream95 for the Vivobook S15
(github.com/icecream95/udev-hid-bpf, commit 519dadad5420). The protocol
of 0B05:4543 matches the A14 one (same report ID, commands and event
codes); the extra init command 5A 05 20 31 00 08 comes from the BPF
program.

Changes compared to v1: Vivobook S15 ID, HID_CONNECT_DEFAULT instead of
report type constants (v1 lost hidraw), DMA safe buffer, work queues for
EC writes from raw_event, brightness_set_blocking, real key release
from the EC release event, no global state, devm resources.

Not for upstream as is. Local patch of the vivobook-s15-fedora project,
requires CONFIG_HID_ASUS_EC=m. Remove the HID-BPF program for this keyboard
when this driver is in use, otherwise Fn-lock and the backlight key are
handled twice.

Assisted-by: LLM (Claude Opus 5.5)
---
